workedExamples.solution_text:
The support has width $11-3=8$, so the constant density is its reciprocal.
$\begin{align*}f(x)&=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{8},&3\le x\le11,\\0,&\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}\end{align*}$
The density is non-negative, and the rectangle has total area
$\begin{align*}A&=(11-3)\times\frac{1}{8}\\&=1.\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-0.4,0) -- (0.35,0);
\draw[->] (0.75,0) -- (6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw (0.35,-0.1) -- (0.55,0.1) (0.55,-0.1) -- (0.75,0.1);
\draw[->] (0,-0.3) -- (0,2.6) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (1,0) -- (1,1.8) -- (5,1.8) -- (5,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,1.8) -- (1,1.8);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$3$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$11$};
\node[left] at (0,1.8) {$\frac{1}{8}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The density is $\frac{1}{10-(-2)}=\frac{1}{12}$ on $[-2,10]$. Each probability is the area of its rectangle.

a.
$\begin{align*}P(1\le X\le5)&=\int_1^5\frac{1}{12}\,dx\\&=\left[\frac{x}{12}\right]_1^5\\&=\frac{5-1}{12}\\&=\frac{1}{3}.\end{align*}$
The shaded rectangle represents this probability.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{probabilityFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[probabilityFill] (0.5,0) rectangle (2.5,1.8);
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.3) -- (0,2.6) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-1,0) -- (-1,1.8) -- (5,1.8) -- (5,0);
\draw[dashed] (0.5,0) -- (0.5,1.8) (2.5,0) -- (2.5,1.8);
\node[below] at (-1,0) {$-2$};
\node[below] at (0.5,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (2.5,0) {$5$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$10$};
\node[above left] at (0,1.8) {$\frac{1}{12}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

b. The lower tail runs from the support boundary $-2$ to $4$.
$\begin{align*}P(X\le4)&=\frac{1}{12}\bigl(4-(-2)\bigr)\\&=\frac{6}{12}\\&=\frac{1}{2}.\end{align*}$

c. The upper tail runs from $7$ to the support boundary $10$.
$\begin{align*}P(X>7)&=\frac{1}{12}(10-7)\\&=\frac{3}{12}\\&=\frac{1}{4}.\end{align*}$
Including or excluding an endpoint gives the same probability because $P(X=7)=0$.

